,["עַד","'ad","H5704","HR","until"],["הַיּוֹם","haiyom","H3117","HTd/Ncmsa","the day"],["הַזֶּה","hazeh","H2088","HTd/Tm","<the> this"]]}},"people":[{"id":"rehoboam_2412","name":"Rehoboam","also":"Roboam","summary":"He enlarges the people, the successor of Solomon on the throne, and apparently his only son. He was the son of Naamah “the Ammonitess,” some well-known Ammonitish princess (1 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 12:13).","verses":42,"father":"Solomon","mother":"Naamah","v":[1,3,6,12,13,17,18]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[2,6]},{"id":"jeroboam_872","name":"Jeroboam","also":"","summary":"The son of Nebat (1 Kings 11:26-39), “an Ephrathite,” the first king of the ten tribes, over whom he reigned twenty-two years (B.C. 976-945).","verses":81,"father":"Nebat","mother":"Zeruah","v":[2,3,12,15]},{"id":"nebat_2165","name":"Nebat","also":"","summary":"Sight; aspect, the father of Jeroboam, the king of Israel (1 Kings 11:26, etc.).","verses":25,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2,15]},{"id":"ahijah_135","name":"Ahijah","also":"","summary":"A prophet of Shiloh (1 Kings 11:29; 14:2), called the “Shilonite,” in the days of Rehoboam. We have on record two of his remarkable prophecies, 1 Kings 11:31-39, announcing the rending of the ten tribes from Solomon; and 1 Kings 14:6-16, delivered to Jeroboam’s wife, foretelling the death of Abijah the king’s son, the destruction of Jeroboam’s house, and the captivity of Israel “beyond the river.”","verses":11,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[16,19]},{"id":"jesse_903","name":"Jesse","also":"","summary":"Firm, or a gift, a son of Obed, the son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:17, 22; Matt. 1:5, 6; Luke 3:32). He was the father of eight sons, the youngest of whom was David (1 Sam. 17:12).","verses":44,"father":"Obed","mother":"","v":[16]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[17,18]},{"id":"adoniram_102","name":"Adoniram","also":"Adoram, Hadoram","summary":"One who was “over the tribute;” i.e., “over the levy.” He was stoned by the Israelites after they had revolted from Rehoboam (2 Chr. 10:18).","verses":5,"father":"Abda","mother":"","v":[18]}],"places":[{"id":"shechem_1069","name":"Shechem","kind":"City","lat":32.22111,"lon":35.25444,"summary":"A city in Samaria (Gen. 33:18), called also Sichem (12:6), Sychem (Acts 7:16). It stood in the narrow sheltered valley between Ebal on the north and Gerizim on the south, these mountains at their base being only some 500 yards apart.","verses":40,"v":[1]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[2]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[18]},{"id":"northern-kingdom-of-israel_1302","name":"Israel","kind":"Region","lat":null,"lon":null,"summary":"Kingdom, -974 to -720 (2Chr.10.19 to 2Kgs.17.6); adde